On Tue, May 31, 2011 at 11:54:00AM -0700, Robin Lee Powell wrote:
> 
> We're playing a simplified Nomic called Fantasy Rules Committee.
> 
> The main rules for FRC are here:
> 
> https://groups.google.com/group/frc-play/web/regular-ordinances-revised-oct-2007
> 
> but that makes them look a lot more complicated than they are;
> here's the super-simplified version:
> 
>   There are real rules and fantasy rules; rounds consist of posting
>   fantasy rules, which must all be consistent with each other; you
>   can only post a fantasy rule if you have in the past week; at the
>   beginning, everyone is considered to have posted; last one capable
>   of posting wins

Sorry, meant to include this before; here's a sample round.  This
round is much longer than most of them; it actually drummed up some
real interest.

Here's the first three:

https://groups.google.com/group/frc-play/browse_thread/thread/2b6d0a783fb0c76c

https://groups.google.com/group/frc-play/browse_thread/thread/bfe010755f7a6559

https://groups.google.com/group/frc-play/browse_thread/thread/a7c343f25369c16f (make
sure to expand quoting on the first message)

Here's the full thread; it starts at the bottom of this page and
goes upwards:

https://groups.google.com/group/frc-play/topics?start=27&sa=N

But the first three give you a sense of the game flow.

Eventually people stop posting on a given theme, due to boredom or
increased complexity, and a round ends and a new one starts a week
after that.

